  "briefing": "An uncharted frontier sector, different every time. Raiders have dug in somewhere on the far side; the Ceres Free Traders hold a port of their own. At peace with you, at war with the raiders.\n\n[b]You arrive with a Colony Ship and a Constructor.[/b] Open your home system (click your fleet, then [b]S[/b]), select a habitable world and found your [b]capital[/b] with the Colony Ship. Nothing is yours until you settle it. Your Constructor then builds mining bases and research stations on the other bodies of a system you hold, or claims an empty system as an outpost. Colonies of 2+ population build more Colony Ships and Constructors; flying a fleet into an empty system claims nothing.\n\n[b]Goal:[/b] outlast your rivals. Win by [b]conquest[/b] (be the last major power), by [b]science[/b] (research Ascension Theory and complete the Ascension Gate; everyone sees it being built) or by [b]score[/b] when the turn limit arrives. [b]E[/b] > Victory shows how close everyone is.\n\n[b]War.[/b] Moving warships into an enemy system always starts a battle against its defenses. Win it and an outpost is yours; a colony also needs a [b]Troop Transport[/b] in your fleet, or you can only [b]blockade[/b] it while you stay. Unescorted civilian ships are destroyed by enemy warships.\n\n[b]Controls[/b]: click a fleet, then a blue hex. [b]S[/b] system map, [b]E[/b] Empire, [b]H[/b] Heroes, [b]D[/b] detach ships, [b]Space[/b] end turn, [b]Esc[/b] menu.",
  "battle_max_rounds": 30,
  "default_battle_map": "open_space",
